# Task API

A simple RESTful CRUD API built with FastAPI for managing tasks. This project was created as part of the FlyRank Backend Internship - Week 2 Assignment A1.

The API stores tasks in memory and supports creating, reading, updating, and deleting tasks. It also includes automatic interactive API documentation using Swagger UI.

## Features

- Create a task
- Get all tasks
- Get a single task by ID
- Update a task
- Delete a task
- Interactive Swagger UI documentation

## Technologies Used

- Python 3.10+
- FastAPI
- Uvicorn

## Installation

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/vicsblu/crud.git
```

Navigate into the project folder:

```bash
cd flyrank-crud-api
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install fastapi uvicorn
```

## Running the Application

Start the server:

```bash
uvicorn main:app --reload
```

The API will be available at:

```
http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

Swagger UI:

```
http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
```

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| GET | / | API information |
| GET | /health | Health check |
| GET | /tasks | Get all tasks |
| GET | /tasks/{id} | Get a task by ID |
| POST | /tasks | Create a new task |
| PUT | /tasks/{id} | Update a task |
| DELETE | /tasks/{id} | Delete a task |

## Example cURL Request

Create a task:

```bash
curl -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:8000/tasks" \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d "{\"title\":\"Learn FastAPI\"}"
```

Example Response:

```json
{
    "id": 4,
    "title": "Learn FastAPI",
    "done": false
}
```

